WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:17.740
Messier 22 or M22, also known as NGC 6656 or the Great Sagittarius Cluster, or less commonly the Crackerjack Cluster, is an elliptical globular cluster of stars in the constellation Sagittarius, near the Galactic bulge region.

00:18.325 --> 00:21.331
It is one of the brightest globulars visible in the night sky.

00:21.853 --> 00:28.903
The brightest stars are 11th magnitude, with hundreds of stars bright enough to resolve with an 8" telescope.

00:29.493 --> 00:38.020
It is just south of the sun's position in mid-December, and northeast of Lambda Sagittarii, the northernmost star of the "Teapot" asterism.
